Hi,

in the previous mail, I forgot the newest one.   (Per request from
Lee) I implemented A52 (aka AC3) output plugin.  This requires
libavcodec of ffmpeg as the encoding engine, thus the plugin itself is
pretty clean and simple.

The plugin encodes 2-6 channel PCM input and outputs the compressed
stream to SPDIF.  When you have an SPDIF output device on your board,
you can try this.  For example, define the below in ~/.asoundrc:

	pcm.a52out {
		type plug
		slave.pcm {
			type upmix
			slave.pcm {
				type a52
			}
		}
	}

then you can play via "a52out" PCM

	% aplay -Da52out foo.wav

See alsa-plugins/doc/a52.txt for details.

BTW, combining this one and dmix is impossible, unfortunately, because
dmix needs the background-DMA transfer but this plugin does explicit 
copying.


Takashi


